module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Groupoids.More.SectionsInfinitesimalDifference
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Thickenings.LiftDifferenceTargetValues
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.DirectImageChartProjection
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ConormalModuleBaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.AffineChartDiagramCover
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ClosedImmersionModulePushforward

/-!
# The two comorphisms of two sections of `Γ₀` agree on the defining ideal of `R₀`

Let `G = (U, R, s, t, c)` be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over a scheme `S`, let `U₀ ⊆ U` be a
first order thickening, let `R₀ = s^{-1}(U₀) ⊆ R` and let `δ₁, δ₂` be two elements of the set
`Γ₀` of [Stacks Project, Tag 0CKB].  Their comorphisms, read through the thickening in the
direct image along `e₀ ≫ j : U₀ ⟶ R`, are two morphisms of sheaves of rings

`𝒪_R ⟶ (e₀ ≫ j)_*(i^{-1}𝒪_U)`

on the small étale site of `R` whose difference takes its values in the square-zero ideal
`(e₀ ≫ j)_*𝒞_{U₀/U}` of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.squareZeroValuesAt`.  This file proves that
**they agree on the defining ideal of `R₀` in `R`**, and transports that to the statement on the
small étale site of `R₀` which is hypothesis (2) of [Stacks Project, Tag 0618] in the groupoid
situation.

The argument is the one the source gives.  The defining ideal of `R₀ = s^{-1}(U₀)` in `R` is,
over every commutative diagram of étale scheme charts over `s` with both charts affine,
generated by the functions pulled back along `s` from the defining ideal of `U₀` in `U`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt_preimage_eq_map_chartDiagram`), and such charts are
cover-dense (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_topology_of_hasAffineChartDiagram`).  On those
generators the two comorphisms agree, because `δ₁` and `δ₂` are sections of one and the same
morphism `s` and have one and the same restriction to `U₀`
(`GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.structureSharp_source_comp_map_structureSharpThroughThickeningAt_eq`),
read chartwise through `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.directImageChartProjection`.  The difference of
the two comorphisms is a derivation for the action through the identity of `𝒪_R`, so
`Stacks.Sites.app_eq_of_app_eq_zero_of_mem_span_of_smul_eq_zero` carries the agreement from the
generators to the whole ideal.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionSharp`: the comorphism of an
  element of `Γ₀`, read through the thickening in the direct image along `e₀ ≫ j`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionValues`: the square-zero
  ideal `(e₀ ≫ j)_*𝒞_{U₀/U}` of `𝒪_R`-modules in which their difference takes its values.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionSharp_app_chartDiagramPullback`:
  **the two comorphisms agree on a function pulled back along `s`** over a commutative diagram
  of étale scheme charts.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionSharp_app_eq_of_app_eq_zero`:
  **the two comorphisms agree on the defining ideal of `R₀` in `R`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app_eq`:
  **hypothesis (2) of [Stacks Project, Tag 0618] in the groupoid situation**: the two
  transported comorphisms on the small étale site of `R₀` agree on the sections killed by
  `j^♯ : j^{-1}𝒪_R ⟶ 𝒪_{R₀}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionLiftDifferenceData`: the
  resulting `Stacks.Sites.LiftDifferenceData`.

## Implementation notes

The two scalar actions on the sections of the ideal of values are written at the canonical ring
sheaf spelling `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite ...).O`, as in the
hypothesis of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.liftDifferenceDataOfHom`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CKE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CKE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CKB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CKB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0618](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0618)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04CP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04CP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03G8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03G8)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPushforward

universe u uu vv

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces

open AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable {C : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : C.Contains S}
  {Bas : AlgebraicSpaces C S hS} (G : GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces C S hS Bas)
  (U₀ : ClosedSubspaces C S hS G.objects.1)

/-- The unit `e₀ : U₀ ⟶ R₀` of the restricted groupoid, followed by the inclusion `j : R₀ ⟶ R`:
the morphism `U₀ ⟶ R` the comorphisms of the elements of `Γ₀` are read in the direct image
along.

It is a `def` and not an `abbrev`, with
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.restrictedUnitArrow_eq` to unfold it by hand:
inlined, it makes the kernel compare the two spellings of a sheaf of rings on the small étale
site of `R` inside terms of the size of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureSharpThroughThickeningAt`, which is a deterministic
timeout. -/
noncomputable def restrictedUnitArrow :
    (⟨U₀.1.toFunctor, U₀.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces C S hS) ⟶ G.arrows :=
  restrictedUnit G U₀ ≫
    subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)

/-- The defining equation of
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.restrictedUnitArrow`. -/
theorem restrictedUnitArrow_eq :
    restrictedUnitArrow G U₀ =
      restrictedUnit G U₀ ≫
        subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀) := rfl

/-- An element of `Γ₀` restricts on `U₀` to `e₀ ≫ j`, with the composite named. -/
theorem comp_eq_restrictedUnitArrow {δ : Section G} (hδ : IsInfinitesimalSection G U₀ δ) :
    subspaceInclusion C S hS G.objects U₀ ≫ δ.1 = restrictedUnitArrow G U₀ :=
  comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ hδ

/-- **The comorphism of an element of `Γ₀`, read through the thickening `U₀ ⊂ U`**, as a
morphism of sheaves of rings `𝒪_R ⟶ (e₀ ≫ j)_*(i^{-1}𝒪_U)` on the small étale site of `R`.

As with `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.restrictedUnitArrow`, this is a `def` with
a `rfl` equation
(`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionSharp_eq`) rather than an
`abbrev`: the defining equation is checked once, in a statement small enough for the kernel to
do it, instead of at every occurrence. -/
noncomputable def infinitesimalSectionSharp (δ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀) :
    structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows ⟶
      thickeningLiftRingSheafAt C S hS U₀ G.arrows (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) :=
  structureSharpThroughThickeningAt C S hS U₀ δ.1.1 (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀)
    (comp_eq_restrictedUnitArrow G U₀ δ.2)

/-- The defining equation of
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionSharp`, with the morphism
`e₀ ≫ j` spelled out. -/
theorem infinitesimalSectionSharp_eq (δ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀) :
    infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ =
      structureSharpThroughThickeningAt C S hS U₀ δ.1.1
        (restrictedUnit G U₀ ≫
          subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))
        (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ.2) := rfl

variable (hU₀ : IsFirstOrderThickening C S hS G.objects U₀.1)

/-- **The square-zero ideal in which the difference of the two comorphisms takes its values**:
the direct image along `e₀ ≫ j` of the conormal module `𝒞_{U₀/U}`, included into
`(e₀ ≫ j)_*(i^{-1}𝒪_U)`. -/
noncomputable abbrev infinitesimalSectionValues :
    Stacks.Sites.SquareZeroValues
      ((modulePushforward C S hS (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀)).obj
        (conormalModule C S hS G.objects U₀)) :=
  squareZeroValuesAt C S hS U₀ G.arrows (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) hU₀

/-! ### The comorphism read through the thickening, after the reduction -/

/-- The reduction of the comorphism of an element of `Γ₀` read through the thickening is the
comorphism of `e₀ ≫ j`.  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureSharpThroughThickeningAt_comp_reduction`. -/
theorem infinitesimalSectionSharp_comp_reduction (δ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀) :
    infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ ≫
        thickeningLiftReductionAt C S hS U₀ G.arrows (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) =
      𝟙 (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows) ≫
        structureSharp C S hS (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) :=
  (structureSharpThroughThickeningAt_comp_reduction C S hS U₀ δ.1.1
    (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) (comp_eq_restrictedUnitArrow G U₀ δ.2)).trans
      (Category.id_comp _).symm

/-- The two comorphisms of two elements of `Γ₀` read through the thickening agree after the
reduction, both being the comorphism of `e₀ ≫ j`. -/
theorem infinitesimalSectionSharp_comp_reduction_eq (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀) :
    infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁ ≫
        thickeningLiftReductionAt C S hS U₀ G.arrows (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) =
      infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂ ≫
        thickeningLiftReductionAt C S hS U₀ G.arrows (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) :=
  structureSharpThroughThickeningAt_comp_reduction_eq C S hS U₀ δ₁.1.1 δ₂.1.1
    (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) (comp_eq_restrictedUnitArrow G U₀ δ₁.2)
    (comp_eq_restrictedUnitArrow G U₀ δ₂.2)

/-! ### A function vanishing on `R₀` kills the ideal of values -/

/-- **A section of `𝒪_R` killed by `j^♯ : 𝒪_R ⟶ j_*𝒪_{R₀}` kills the ideal of values.**  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smul_modulePushforward_comp_eq_zero` at the factorization
`e₀ ≫ j` of the morphism the ideal of values is the direct image along. -/
theorem smul_infinitesimalSectionValues_eq_zero
    (V : (Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1)ᵒᵖ)
    (z : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj V))
    (hz : (structureSharp C S hS
      (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app V z = 0)
    (m : ((modulePushforward C S hS (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀)).obj
      (conormalModule C S hS G.objects U₀)).val.obj V) :
    @HSMul.hSMul
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite C S hS G.arrows.1 G.arrows.2).O).obj.obj V)
      _ _ _ z m = 0 :=
  smul_modulePushforward_comp_eq_zero C S hS (restrictedUnit G U₀)
    (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))
    (conormalModule C S hS G.objects U₀) V z hz m

/-! ### The two comorphisms agree on the functions pulled back along the source -/

/-- The agreement of the two comorphisms after the comorphism of the source, with the
direct image written in the form the chart projections of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/DirectImageChartProjection.lean` are stated for. -/
theorem structureSharp_source_comp_map_infinitesimalSectionSharp_eq
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀) :
    structureSharp C S hS G.source ≫
        pullbackRingSheafMap (Space.SmallEtale.topology C S hS G.objects.1)
          (smallEtaleDirectImage C S hS G.source) (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁) =
      structureSharp C S hS G.source ≫
        pullbackRingSheafMap (Space.SmallEtale.topology C S hS G.objects.1)
          (smallEtaleDirectImage C S hS G.source) (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂) :=
  structureSharp_source_comp_map_structureSharpThroughThickeningAt_eq G U₀ δ₁ δ₂

/-- **The two comorphisms of two elements of `Γ₀` agree on a regular function pulled back along
the source**, over a commutative diagram of étale scheme charts over `s`.

This is the part of Equation [Stacks Project, Tag 0CKE] which is not formal. -/
theorem infinitesimalSectionSharp_app_chartDiagramPullback
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    (d : ChartDiagram C S hS G.arrows.1 G.objects.1 G.source.hom)
    (b : (structureSetSheaf C S hS G.objects).obj.obj (op d.V)) :
    (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁).hom.app (op d.U)
        ((chartDiagramPullback C S hS G.source d).hom b) =
      (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂).hom.app (op d.U)
        ((chartDiagramPullback C S hS G.source d).hom b) := by
  rw [app_chartDiagramPullback_eq_directImageChartProjection C S hS G.source d
      (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁) b,
    app_chartDiagramPullback_eq_directImageChartProjection C S hS G.source d
      (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂) b]
  exact congrArg ((directImageChartProjection C S hS G.source d.V
      (StructuredArrow.mk (Y := op d.U)
        (baseChangeArrowOfChartDiagram C S hS G.source d).op)).app _)
    (ringSheafHom_congr_app_apply
      (structureSharp_source_comp_map_infinitesimalSectionSharp_eq G U₀ δ₁ δ₂) (op d.V) b)

/-! ### Local generators of the defining ideal of `R₀` on which the two comorphisms agree -/

/-- **The generating family.**  The regular functions on an étale chart of `R` which vanish on
`R₀ = s^{-1}(U₀)` and at which the two comorphisms of `δ₁` and `δ₂`, read through the thickening
`U₀ ⊂ U`, agree. -/
def infinitesimalSectionAgreement (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    (Y : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1) :
    Set (ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op Y))) :=
  {y | (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
        (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app (op Y) y = 0 ∧
    (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁).hom.app (op Y) y =
      (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂).hom.app (op Y) y}

/-- Membership in the generating family unfolded.  It is a `def` rather than an `abbrev` so
that the kernel compares two instances of it by comparing their arguments instead of their
bodies, which mention the two comorphisms. -/
theorem mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreement_iff (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    (Y : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1)
    (y : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op Y))) :
    y ∈ infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ Y ↔
      ((structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
          (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app (op Y) y = 0 ∧
        (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁).hom.app (op Y) y =
          (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂).hom.app (op Y) y) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- A morphism of sheaves of rings commutes with restriction, read on sections.  Stated with
both sheaves implicit, as `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ringSheafHom_congr_app_apply` is. -/
private theorem ringSheafHom_naturality_apply {Cc : Type uu} [Category.{vv} Cc]
    {Jc : GrothendieckTopology Cc} {A Bb : Sheaf Jc RingCat.{u}} (φ : A ⟶ Bb)
    {V W : Ccᵒᵖ} (p : V ⟶ W) (y : A.obj.obj V) :
    φ.hom.app W (A.obj.map p y) = Bb.obj.map p (φ.hom.app V y) :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (φ.hom.naturality p) y

/-- **The generating family is stable under étale restriction**, both conditions being equations
between morphisms of sheaves read on sections. -/
theorem map_mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreement (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {Y Y' : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1} (p : Y' ⟶ Y)
    {y : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op Y))}
    (hy : y ∈ infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ Y) :
    (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map p.op y ∈
      infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ Y' :=
  (mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreement_iff G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ Y' _).2
    ⟨by rw [ringSheafHom_naturality_apply, hy.1, map_zero],
      by rw [ringSheafHom_naturality_apply, ringSheafHom_naturality_apply, hy.2]⟩

/-- **The ideal generated by the family is stable under étale restriction.**  Restriction is a
ring homomorphism, and the family is stable, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.map_mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreement`. -/
theorem map_mem_span_infinitesimalSectionAgreement (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {Y Y' : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1} (p : Y' ⟶ Y)
    {r : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op Y))}
    (hr : r ∈ Ideal.span (infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ Y)) :
    (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map p.op r ∈
      Ideal.span (infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ Y') := by
  induction hr using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy => exact Ideal.subset_span (map_mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ p hy)
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ ha hb
  | smul c a _ ha => rw [smul_eq_mul, map_mul]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ ha

/-- **A function pulled back along `s` from the defining ideal of `U₀` belongs to the generating
family.** -/
theorem chartDiagramPullback_mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreement
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    (d : ChartDiagram C S hS G.arrows.1 G.objects.1 G.source.hom)
    [IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme C S hS).obj d.V.1.left)]
    [IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme C S hS).obj d.U.1.left)]
    {b : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.objects).obj.obj (op d.V))}
    (hb : b ∈ definingIdealAt C S hS G.objects U₀ (op d.V)) :
    (chartDiagramPullback C S hS G.source d).hom b ∈
      infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ d.U :=
  (mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreement_iff G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ d.U _).2
    ⟨(mem_definingIdealAt_iff C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀) (op d.U)
          _).1
        ((definingIdealAt_preimage_eq_map_chartDiagram C S hS G.source U₀ d).ge
          (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hb)),
      infinitesimalSectionSharp_app_chartDiagramPullback G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ d b⟩

/-- **The sieve of arrows over which the restricted section lies in the ideal generated by the
family.**  It is a sieve because the family is stable under étale restriction, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.map_mem_span_infinitesimalSectionAgreement`. -/
def infinitesimalSectionAgreementSieve (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {V : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op V))) : Sieve V where
  arrows {Y} p := (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map p.op x ∈
    Ideal.span (infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ Y)
  downward_closed {Y Z} {f} hf g := by
    show (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map (f.op ≫ g.op) x ∈
      Ideal.span (infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ Z)
    rw [(structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map_comp_apply f.op g.op x]
    exact map_mem_span_infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ g hf

/-- **A section of `𝒪_R` vanishing on `R₀` still vanishes on `R₀` after étale restriction**: the
comorphism of the inclusion `j : R₀ ⟶ R` commutes with restriction. -/
theorem structureSharp_preimage_app_map_eq_zero
    {Y Y' : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1} (p : Y' ⟶ Y)
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op Y)))
    (hx : (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app (op Y) x = 0) :
    (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
        (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app (op Y')
        ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map p.op x) = 0 :=
  by rw [ringSheafHom_naturality_apply, hx, map_zero]

/-- The restriction of a section of `𝒪_R` vanishing on `R₀` lies in the defining ideal of `R₀`
at the smaller chart. -/
theorem map_mem_definingIdealAt_preimage
    {Y Y' : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1} (p : Y' ⟶ Y)
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op Y)))
    (hx : (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app (op Y) x = 0) :
    (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map p.op x ∈
      definingIdealAt C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀) (op Y') :=
  (mem_definingIdealAt_iff C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀) (op Y')
      ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map p.op x)).2
    (structureSharp_preimage_app_map_eq_zero G U₀ p x hx)

/-- **At an affine chart diagram over `s`, the defining ideal of `R₀` is contained in the ideal
generated by the family.**  The defining ideal of `R₀ = s^{-1}(U₀)` at such a chart is generated
by the pullbacks along `s` of the sections of the defining ideal of `U₀`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt_preimage_eq_map_chartDiagram`, and each of those
pullbacks is in the family. -/
theorem definingIdealAt_preimage_le_span_infinitesimalSectionAgreement
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    (d : ChartDiagram C S hS G.arrows.1 G.objects.1 G.source.hom)
    [IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme C S hS).obj d.V.1.left)]
    [IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme C S hS).obj d.U.1.left)] :
    definingIdealAt C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀) (op d.U) ≤
      Ideal.span (infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ d.U) :=
  (definingIdealAt_preimage_eq_map_chartDiagram C S hS G.source U₀ d).le.trans
    (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 (fun y hy => Ideal.mem_comap.2 (Ideal.subset_span
      (chartDiagramPullback_mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ d hy))))

/-- **The commutative diagram of étale scheme charts over `s` carried by a chart with an affine
chart diagram.**  Naming it keeps the anonymous constructor out of the applications below, whose
terms the kernel otherwise has to reduce through. -/
noncomputable def affineChartDiagram {W : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1}
    (hW : HasAffineChartDiagram C S hS G.source W) :
    ChartDiagram C S hS G.arrows.1 G.objects.1 G.source.hom where
  U := W
  V := hW.2.choose
  g := hW.2.choose_spec.choose
  comm := (hW.2.choose_spec.choose_spec.1).symm

/-- The chart of `R` of the diagram is the given chart. -/
theorem affineChartDiagram_U {W : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1}
    (hW : HasAffineChartDiagram C S hS G.source W) : (affineChartDiagram G hW).U = W := rfl

/-- The chart of `R` of the affine chart diagram is affine. -/
instance isAffine_affineChartDiagram_U {W : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1}
    (hW : HasAffineChartDiagram C S hS G.source W) :
    IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme C S hS).obj (affineChartDiagram G hW).U.1.left) := hW.1

/-- The chart of `U` of the affine chart diagram is affine. -/
instance isAffine_affineChartDiagram_V {W : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1}
    (hW : HasAffineChartDiagram C S hS G.source W) :
    IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme C S hS).obj (affineChartDiagram G hW).V.1.left) :=
  hW.2.choose_spec.choose_spec.2

/-- **Over the chart of an affine chart diagram over `s`, a section vanishing on `R₀` lies in
the ideal generated by the family.** -/
theorem mem_span_infinitesimalSectionAgreement_of_chartDiagram
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {Y : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op Y)))
    (hx : (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app (op Y) x = 0)
    (d : ChartDiagram C S hS G.arrows.1 G.objects.1 G.source.hom)
    [IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme C S hS).obj d.V.1.left)]
    [IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme C S hS).obj d.U.1.left)]
    (a : d.U ⟶ Y) :
    (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map a.op x ∈
      Ideal.span (infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ d.U) :=
  definingIdealAt_preimage_le_span_infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ d
    (map_mem_definingIdealAt_preimage G U₀ a x hx)

/-- Every chart carrying an affine chart diagram over `s` is in the sieve. -/
theorem hasAffineChartDiagram_mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreementSieve
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {V : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op V)))
    (hx : (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app (op V) x = 0)
    ⦃W : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1⦄ (a : W ⟶ V)
    (hW : HasAffineChartDiagram C S hS G.source W) :
    infinitesimalSectionAgreementSieve G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ x a :=
  mem_span_infinitesimalSectionAgreement_of_chartDiagram G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ x hx
    (affineChartDiagram G hW) a

/-- **The sieve is a covering sieve**, the charts carrying an affine chart diagram over `s`
being cover-dense by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_topology_of_hasAffineChartDiagram`. -/
theorem infinitesimalSectionAgreementSieve_mem_topology
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {V : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op V)))
    (hx : (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app (op V) x = 0) :
    infinitesimalSectionAgreementSieve G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ x ∈
      Space.SmallEtale.topology C S hS G.arrows.1 V :=
  mem_topology_of_hasAffineChartDiagram C S hS G.source V _
    (hasAffineChartDiagram_mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreementSieve G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ x hx)

/-- **The defining ideal of `R₀` in `R` is locally generated by functions at which the two
comorphisms agree.**  This is the hypothesis `hgen` of
`Stacks.Sites.app_eq_of_app_eq_zero_of_mem_span_of_smul_eq_zero`. -/
theorem exists_mem_span_infinitesimalSectionAgreement (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {V : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj (op V)))
    (hx : (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app (op V) x = 0) :
    ∃ T : Sieve V, T ∈ Space.SmallEtale.topology C S hS G.arrows.1 V ∧
      ∀ ⦃Y : Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1⦄ (p : Y ⟶ V), T p →
        (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.map p.op x ∈
          Ideal.span (infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ Y) :=
  ⟨infinitesimalSectionAgreementSieve G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ x,
    infinitesimalSectionAgreementSieve_mem_topology G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ x hx,
    fun _ _ hp => hp⟩

/-! ### The two comorphisms agree on the defining ideal of `R₀` -/

include hU₀ in
/-- The sectionwise difference of the two comorphisms, read in the ideal of values. -/
noncomputable def infinitesimalSectionDiffValue (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {V : (Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1)ᵒᵖ}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj V)) :
    ((modulePushforward C S hS (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀)).obj
      (conormalModule C S hS G.objects U₀)).val.obj V :=
  sharpDiffAt C S hS U₀ G.arrows (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) hU₀
    (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁) (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂)
    (infinitesimalSectionSharp_comp_reduction_eq G U₀ δ₁ δ₂) x

/-- The defining equation of
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionDiffValue`. -/
theorem squareZeroValuesAt_ι_infinitesimalSectionDiffValue
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {V : (Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1)ᵒᵖ}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj V)) :
    (infinitesimalSectionValues G U₀ hU₀).ι
        (infinitesimalSectionDiffValue G U₀ hU₀ δ₁ δ₂ x) =
      (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁).hom.app V x -
        (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂).hom.app V x :=
  squareZeroValuesAt_ι_sharpDiffAt C S hS U₀ G.arrows (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) hU₀
    (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁) (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂)
    (infinitesimalSectionSharp_comp_reduction_eq G U₀ δ₁ δ₂) x

/-- The `𝒪_R`-action on the ideal of values is multiplication by the comorphism of `δ₁`. -/
theorem infinitesimalSectionValues_ι_smul (δ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {V : (Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1)ᵒᵖ}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj V))
    (m : ((modulePushforward C S hS (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀)).obj
      (conormalModule C S hS G.objects U₀)).val.obj V) :
    (infinitesimalSectionValues G U₀ hU₀).ι
        (@HSMul.hSMul
          ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
            (smallEtaleRingedSite C S hS G.arrows.1 G.arrows.2).O).obj.obj V)
          _ _ _
          ((𝟙 (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows) :
            structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows ⟶ structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).hom.app V x)
          m) =
      (show ToType ((infinitesimalSectionValues G U₀ hU₀).ambient.obj.obj V) from
          (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ).hom.app V x) *
        (infinitesimalSectionValues G U₀ hU₀).ι m :=
  squareZeroValuesAt_ι_smul C S hS U₀ G.arrows (restrictedUnitArrow G U₀) hU₀
    (𝟙 (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows)) (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ)
    (infinitesimalSectionSharp_comp_reduction G U₀ δ) x m

include hU₀ in
/-- **The two comorphisms of two elements of `Γ₀` agree on the defining ideal of `R₀` in `R`.**
Their sectionwise difference takes its values in the square-zero ideal `(e₀ ≫ j)_*𝒞_{U₀/U}`, so
it is a derivation for the action of `𝒪_R` on that ideal; that action factors through the
comorphism of `e₀ ≫ j`, hence is killed by the defining ideal of `R₀`; and the defining ideal
is locally generated by functions at which the two comorphisms agree.

This is `Stacks.Sites.app_eq_of_app_eq_zero_of_mem_span_of_smul_eq_zero` at the data assembled
above, and it is the geometric heart of Equation [Stacks Project, Tag 0CKE]. -/
theorem infinitesimalSectionSharp_app_eq_of_app_eq_zero (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {V : (Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1)ᵒᵖ}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj V))
    (hx : (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app V x = 0) :
    (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁).hom.app V x =
      (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂).hom.app V x :=
  Stacks.Sites.app_eq_of_app_eq_zero_of_mem_span_of_smul_eq_zero
    (q := 𝟙 (structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows))
    (q' := structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)))
    (infinitesimalSectionValues G U₀ hU₀)
    (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₁) (infinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ₂)
    (fun {_} y m => infinitesimalSectionValues_ι_smul G U₀ hU₀ δ₁ y m)
    (fun {_} y => infinitesimalSectionDiffValue G U₀ hU₀ δ₁ δ₂ y)
    (fun {_} y => squareZeroValuesAt_ι_infinitesimalSectionDiffValue G U₀ hU₀ δ₁ δ₂ y)
    (fun {_} z hz m => smul_infinitesimalSectionValues_eq_zero G U₀ _ z hz m)
    (fun {_} y hy => Exists.imp (fun _ h => ⟨h.1, fun _ p hp =>
        Ideal.span_mono
          (fun _ hw => (mem_infinitesimalSectionAgreement_iff G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ _ _).1 hw)
          (h.2 p hp)⟩)
      (exists_mem_span_infinitesimalSectionAgreement G U₀ δ₁ δ₂ y hy))
    x hx

include hU₀ in
/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionSharp_app_eq_of_app_eq_zero`
with the morphism `e₀ ≫ j` spelled out, which is the spelling the transported comorphism of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening` is stated at. -/
theorem structureSharpThroughThickeningAt_app_eq_of_app_eq_zero
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    {V : (Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1)ᵒᵖ}
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj V))
    (hx : (structureSharp C S hS (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app V x = 0) :
    (structureSharpThroughThickeningAt C S hS U₀ δ₁.1.1
          (restrictedUnit G U₀ ≫
            subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))
          (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ₁.2)).hom.app V x =
      (structureSharpThroughThickeningAt C S hS U₀ δ₂.1.1
          (restrictedUnit G U₀ ≫
            subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))
          (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ₂.2)).hom.app V x := by
  rw [← infinitesimalSectionSharp_eq G U₀ δ₁, ← infinitesimalSectionSharp_eq G U₀ δ₂]
  exact infinitesimalSectionSharp_app_eq_of_app_eq_zero G U₀ hU₀ δ₁ δ₂ x hx

/-! ### The comorphism transported to the small étale site of `R₀` -/

/-- **The comorphism of an element of `Γ₀` transported to the small étale site of `R₀`**, as a
morphism of sheaves of rings `j^{-1}𝒪_R ⟶ (e₀)_*(i^{-1}𝒪_U)`.  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedSharpThroughThickening` in the groupoid situation; its source
carries the quotient map `j^♯ : j^{-1}𝒪_R ⟶ 𝒪_{R₀}` which the difference of two of them
descends along.

It is a `def` with a `rfl` equation for the same reason as
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionSharp`. -/
noncomputable def restrictedInfinitesimalSectionSharp (δ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀) :
    structureRingSheafInverseImage C S hS
        (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)) ⟶
      restrictedThickeningLiftRingSheaf C S hS U₀
        (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀) (restrictedUnit G U₀) :=
  restrictedSharpThroughThickening C S hS U₀ (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)
    δ.1.1 (restrictedUnit G U₀) (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ.2)

/-- The defining equation of
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.restrictedInfinitesimalSectionSharp`. -/
theorem restrictedInfinitesimalSectionSharp_eq (δ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀) :
    restrictedInfinitesimalSectionSharp G U₀ δ =
      restrictedSharpThroughThickening C S hS U₀ (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)
        δ.1.1 (restrictedUnit G U₀) (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ.2) := rfl

/-- **The defining adjunction identity of the transport, at a section.**  The unit of
`j^{-1} ⊣ j_*` followed by the direct image of the transported comorphism is the comorphism read
in the direct image along `e₀ ≫ j`, through the comparison of iterated direct images; this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ringUnit_comp_map_restrictedSharpThroughThickening` read on a section of
`𝒪_R`. -/
theorem ringUnit_comp_map_restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app
    (δ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀) (V : (Space.SmallEtale C S hS G.arrows.1)ᵒᵖ)
    (a : ToType ((structureRingSheaf C S hS G.arrows).obj.obj V)) :
    (thickeningRingUnit C S hS (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀) ≫
        (pushforwardRingFunctor (smallToposMorphismTypeU C S hS
          (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
            (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)))).map
          (restrictedSharpThroughThickening C S hS U₀
            (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀) δ.1.1 (restrictedUnit G U₀)
            (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ.2))).hom.app V a =
      (structureSharpThroughThickeningAt C S hS U₀ δ.1.1
          (restrictedUnit G U₀ ≫
            subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))
          (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ.2) ≫
        pushforwardRingSheafCompInv C S hS (restrictedUnit G U₀)
          (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))
          (structureRingSheafInverseImage C S hS
            (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.objects U₀))).hom.app V a :=
  ringSheafHom_congr_app_apply
    (ringUnit_comp_map_restrictedSharpThroughThickening C S hS U₀
      (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀) δ.1.1 (restrictedUnit G U₀)
      (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ.2)) V a

include hU₀ in
/-- **Hypothesis (2) of [Stacks Project, Tag 0618] in the groupoid situation.**  The two
transported comorphisms on the small étale site of `R₀` agree on the sections killed by
`j^♯ : j^{-1}𝒪_R ⟶ 𝒪_{R₀}`.

This is the general descent
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.app_eq_of_app_eq_zero_of_app_thickeningRingUnit_eq` at the two
transports: on the small étale site of `R` the two direct images agree at the unit of every
section of `𝒪_R` vanishing on `R₀`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.infinitesimalSectionSharp_app_eq_of_app_eq_zero`
read through the adjunction identity above, and the direct image along the closed immersion `j`
is faithful. -/
theorem restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app_eq (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀)
    (V : (Space.SmallEtale C S hS
      (⟨(preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀).1.toFunctor,
        (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀).2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces C S hS).1)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : ToType ((structureRingSheafInverseImage C S hS
      (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
        (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).obj.obj V))
    (hx : (structureSharpRingInverseImage C S hS
      (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows
        (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))).hom.app V x = 0) :
    (restrictedSharpThroughThickening C S hS U₀ (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)
          δ₁.1.1 (restrictedUnit G U₀) (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ₁.2)).hom.app V x =
      (restrictedSharpThroughThickening C S hS U₀ (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)
          δ₂.1.1 (restrictedUnit G U₀) (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ₂.2)).hom.app V x :=
  app_eq_of_app_eq_zero_of_app_thickeningRingUnit_eq C S hS
    (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)
    (isFirstOrderThickening_restrictedArrows G U₀ hU₀) _ _
    (fun V' a ha => by
      rw [ringUnit_comp_map_restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app G U₀ δ₁,
        ringUnit_comp_map_restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app G U₀ δ₂]
      exact congrArg ((pushforwardRingSheafCompInv C S hS (restrictedUnit G U₀)
          (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀))
          (structureRingSheafInverseImage C S hS
            (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.objects U₀))).hom.app V')
        (structureSharpThroughThickeningAt_app_eq_of_app_eq_zero G U₀ hU₀ δ₁ δ₂ a ha))
    V x hx

include hU₀ in
/-- **The difference of the two transported comorphisms, as the datum the descent consumes.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedLiftDifferenceData` in the groupoid situation, with
hypothesis (2) of [Stacks Project, Tag 0618] discharged by
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces.restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app_eq`. -/
noncomputable def infinitesimalSectionLiftDifferenceData
    (δ₁ δ₂ : InfinitesimalSections G U₀) :
    Stacks.Sites.LiftDifferenceData
      (structureSharpRingInverseImage C S hS
        (subspaceInclusion C S hS G.arrows (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)))
      (restrictedSquareZeroValues C S hS U₀ (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)
        (restrictedUnit G U₀) hU₀) :=
  restrictedLiftDifferenceData C S hS U₀ (preimageSubspace C S hS G.source U₀)
    (restrictedUnit G U₀) hU₀ δ₁.1.1 δ₂.1.1
    (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ₁.2) (comp_eq_restrictedUnit_comp G U₀ δ₂.2)
    (restrictedSharpThroughThickening_app_eq G U₀ hU₀ δ₁ δ₂)

